---
title: Porcupines
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Meat, Poultry, Fish
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@ground beef{1%lb}
@water{1/2%c}
@salt{1%tsp}
@garlic powder{1/8%tsp}
@rice{1/2%c}
@chopped onion{1/3%c}
@celery salt{1/2%tsp}
@pepper{1/8%tsp}
@tomato sauce{1%15-oz can}
@water{1%c}
@Worcestershire sauce{2%tsp}
@grease

Mix together @ground beef{1%lb}, @water{1/2%c}, @salt{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/8%tsp}, @rice{1/2%c}, @chopped onion{1/3%c}, @celery salt{1/2%tsp}, and @pepper{1/8%tsp} and shape into balls. Brown in small amount of grease in skillet. Drain off excess fat.

Stir together @tomato sauce{1%15-oz can}, @water{1%c}, and @Worcestershire sauce{2%tsp}. Pour over meatballs. Reduce heat, cover and simmer for 45 minutes. If necessary, add a small amount of water during cooking.
